6. Cost (ledger S2.21 and S2.29, GNU 14.3 to 14.6 ms per gc3 collection, CPU 11): the scan costs 9.9 M Ir of a 57.5 M collection on batch D, 0.3 M (pure) and 0.4 M (hybrid) of 48.0 M; the conservative-cost check 1.16 on D, 1.03 on both.

Verdict: pure is clean wherever it was exercised, and indistinguishable from the hybrid in cost (ledger S2.29: scan 0.3 M and 0.4 M Ir of a 48 M collection).
Not proven: a producer outside these runs that reads a string through a data pointer after a collection.  If one is found, the repair is to decode the legacy
view's header from its capacity word (flag bit 61 or 62) and mark that string; tools/ai/integ-wh-gc-hybrid.patch turns the tree into the hybrid for a comparison.
